## 4. Content Model

### products.json

Schema per work item:
- `title`, `company`, `year`, `location`
- `tagline`, `description`
- `stats[]` — `{label, value}`
- `url` — links to app or case study
- `flagship: true` — if it should render as a flagship card

### labs.json

Top-level keys:
- `meta` — `{eyebrow, title, intro, statLabs, statProducts, statYears}`
- `labs[]` — array of lab objects

Lab object:
- `id`, `name`, `glyph`, `desc`, `disciplines[]`
- `flagship: true` — if it's a flagship case study
- `products[]` — array of product objects

Product object (standard + case-study fields):
- Standard: `id`, `name`, `tagline`, `what`, `features[]`, `role`, `year`, `stage2`, `stack[]`, `url`
- Case study: `why`, `users[]`, `mvp[]`, `testing`, `next`
- `artifacts[]` — array of artifact objects by kind:
  - `prd` — `{goal, users[], mvp[], nongoals[], label, tags[]}`
  - `flow` — `{steps[], label, tags[]}`
  - `metrics` — `{business, drivers[], product[], label, tags[]}`
  - `workflow` — `{steps[], label, tags[]}`
  - `beforeafter` — `{before, after, label, tags[]}`
  - `screens` — `{items[{name, img?}], label, tags[]}`

### about.json

- `identity` — `{name, title, location, bio}`
- `timeline[]` — `{year, role, company, note}`
- `principles[]` — `{title, body}`
- `skills[]` — `{category, items[]}`

### contact.json

- `email`
- `links[]` — `{label, url, type}`

