## 6. Admin CMS — Current State (v1)

Single file: `admin.html` (682 lines)

### Capabilities
- Password-gated (localStorage token, plaintext password — to be hashed in Phase F)
- Tabs: Site Identity · Work · Labs · About · Contact
- LocalStorage draft persistence
- GitHub Contents API: PUT files, upload images (base64), commit to main
- Offline JSON export fallback
- Form rendering: 5 bespoke `render*()` functions (~200 lines of form code)

### GitHub integration (~150 lines)
- `ghApi(method, path, body)` — wrapper with Bearer token
- `ghGetFile(path)` — GET file + sha
- `putFile(path, content, sha, msg)` — PUT commit
- Token stored in: localStorage key `ghToken`
- Token value: in macOS Keychain as `atlassian-jira-token` (same keychain, separate entry)

### Known limitations
- No delete operations (can PUT but not DELETE or tree-delete)
- No section/page structure management
- No publish diff/preview
- No artifact editing for labs case studies
- Plaintext password in source

---

## 7. Admin v2 Plan — 6 Phases, 7.5 Sessions

This is the approved build plan. Phases are independent and each ships a deployable slice.

### Phase A — Data Liberation (~1.5 sessions)
Move page structure (hero, sections, nav, footer) from HTML into `site.json`.
- Design `site.json` schema
- Rewrite `site.js`, `products.html`, `labs.html`, `about.html`, `contact.html` to render from JSON
- Add raw-JSON temp editor to admin
- Exit: 4 pages render from data, visually identical

### Phase B — Form Engine (~1 session)
Replace 5 bespoke form-render functions with one schema-driven renderer.
- `FormEngine` class (~200 lines)
- `schemas.js` — content model for all types
- Port all tabs onto schemas
- Exit: all CRUD operations work through FormEngine, ~200 lines of old code deleted

### Phase C — Structure Manager — Pages Tab (~1.5 sessions)
New admin tab: drag/hide/add/reorder/delete sections + nav manager + page manager.
- Drag-drop section stack (hand-coded, no Sortable.js)
- Add-section picker with type library
- Nav manager (drag, add/delete nav items)
- Page add/rename/delete
- All wired to site.json drafts
- Exit: restructure site without touching code

### Phase D — Publisher v2 (~1.5 sessions)
Delete operations, atomic folder deletes, cascade dialogs, orphan detector.
- `ghDelete(path, sha)` — single file
- `ghDeleteTree(dir)` — Git Data API atomic folder delete
- Files tab: browse + delete assets/screenshots/apps/case-studies
- Orphan detector: repo structure vs JSON references
- Cascade-delete dialog: one confirm, one batch commit
- Error handling: rate limit, SHA conflict, offline

### Phase E — Preview & Diff (~1 session)
Draft preview on public pages + publish change summary.
- `?preview=1` query param reads from localStorage drafts (all public renderers)
- Deep-diff function: draft vs last-fetched JSON
- Publish-confirmation dialog with file summary + key-level diff

### Phase F — Hardening & Docs (~0.5 sessions)
- Hash the admin password (SHA-256 or bcryptjs)
- Comprehensive GitHub error handling
- `ADMIN_GUIDE.md`
- Full smoke test at desktop + 375px

### Supabase layer — DONE (auth live, drafts ready to wire)
- ✅ Auth: Supabase email/password replaces plaintext password — confirmed working
- ✅ `js/supabase-client.js`: `SB.*` API surface live in browser (`isReady: true`)
- ✅ `supabase/schema.sql`: `cms_content` table + `portfolio-assets` bucket created
- ✅ Admin login: email + password form, `SB.signIn()` first, legacy fallback removed next
- Next: wire `SB.saveDraft` / `SB.loadDraft` into admin's draft persistence (replaces localStorage)
- Future: multi-user workspace, analytics via `portfolio_events` table

### Total: ~8.5 sessions (7.5 core + 1 Supabase)

---

## 8. Supabase Integration Plan

### What it replaces/augments
| Current | With Supabase | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Plaintext password in source | Supabase Auth (email + password) | ✅ Live |
| localStorage drafts | `cms_content` table (`draft_*` rows) | ⬜ Next |
| No analytics | Future: `portfolio_events` table | ⬜ Future |
| Single-user only | Future: multi-user workspaces | ⬜ Future |

### Tables to create in Supabase

```sql
-- Drafts table
create table portfolio_drafts (
  id uuid default gen_random_uuid() primary key,
  user_id uuid references auth.users not null,
  file_key text not null,       -- e.g. 'products', 'labs', 'about', 'contact', 'site'
  content jsonb not null,
  updated_at timestamptz default now()
);
alter table portfolio_drafts enable row level security;
create policy "Users own their drafts"
  on portfolio_drafts for all using (auth.uid() = user_id);
create unique index on portfolio_drafts(user_id, file_key);

-- Events table (future analytics)
create table portfolio_events (
  id bigint generated always as identity primary key,
  event text not null,
  metadata jsonb,
  created_at timestamptz default now()
);
```

### Environment config
Set in admin.html (or a `.env` if moving to a build pipeline):
```
SUPABASE_URL = https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = <your-anon-key>
```

### Connection module
`js/supabase-client.js` — see that file for the full API surface.

